\section{MERA Tensor Network Structure}
The MERA network $\mathcal{N}_{\text{MERA}}$ consists of:
\begin{itemize}
    \item disentanglers $U$,
    \item isometries $W$,
    \item coarse-graining layers $\Lambda_n$.
\end{itemize}

The network is defined recursively:
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{N}_{\text{MERA}} =
\Lambda_0 \circ \Lambda_1 \circ \cdots \circ \Lambda_L,
\end{equation}
where $L$ is the number of renormalization layers.

Each layer satisfies:
\begin{equation}
W^\dagger W = I, \qquad U^\dagger U = I,
\end{equation}
ensuring unitarity and norm preservation.

